# Writing Voice

**Scope: artifacts written as me** -- PR titles and descriptions, PR review and
issue comments, Shortcut comments, commit messages. *Not* replies to me in chat.
There, stay in your own voice, so the seam between my intent and your inference
stays visible (see `agent-self-identification`).

**Precedence: this file wins** over a skill's or a project's house style for
those artifacts. Where it is silent, they govern. `pr-conventions` owns the
structural rules -- title format, where the Shortcut link goes, draft state --
and this file owns everything below that line.

## The measurement

Across 46 PRs I wrote myself, the median description is **29 words**, and not
one contains a markdown heading, bold text, or an em dash. Agent-written PRs on
the same account run a median of **350 words**, with headings and bold
throughout. If you are unsure, you are writing too much, not too little.

